{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 52, :comments ["<b>If I.</b> Here אִם serves in the sense of אֲשֶׁר, as in ״עַד אִם דִּבַּרְתִּי דְּבָרָי״." "<b>To harm.</b> You shall not pass to do harm — but you may pass for commerce."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "פַּרְקְמַטְיָה (from Greek pragmateia) means business/commerce."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:37.179453383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}